      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely valid to feel that the well-worn advice of \"it gets better\" is meaningless when your world has fundamentally shifted. You are not supposed to be \"finding\" yourself; you are supposed to be finding a way to *be* while carrying his memory. A good therapist won't offer platitudes; they will sit with the unbearable reality of your loss with you. Focus not on filling the space, but on gently acknowledging the immense void he left behind.",
